## 2. Implementation written (production files only, no test edited)

Files touched:

1. `apps/www-reading-advantage/src/components/marketing/tutor-commission-calculator.tsx`
   - `shareOfGross` became `shareOfNetwork`; the divisor is `result.networkVolume`.
   - Leg bars use `shareOfNetwork(leg.volume)`; the own bar uses `result.ownVolume`.
   - The own bar value under `graph.ownBar` is `formatMoney(result.ownVolume)`.
   - `onLegCountChange` skips the resize when the field is empty, so the leg rows
     and the typed students stay. A number still resizes. `resizeLegs` keeps the
     earlier typed values when the count grows again.
   - `readLegCount` keeps the add/remove buttons from wiping rows while the field
     is empty.
2. `apps/www-reading-advantage/src/app/[locale]/(marketing)/products/tutor-advantage/page.tsx`
   - `key` widened to `(k: string, values?: Record<string, unknown>) => string`.
   - `legBar: key("calculator.graph.legBar", { n: "{n}" })` (design rule 11).
   - The hero `ProductPicture` gets `priority`.
3. `apps/www-reading-advantage/src/components/products/product-picture.tsx`
   - Optional `priority?: boolean` prop passed to `next/image`.
   - Next 16.4.1 omits the `loading` attribute when `priority` is set
     (`get-img-props.js` line 236 and 446: `isLazy` false leaves `loading` undefined).
     The hero also needs `loading="eager"` to satisfy AC-23 in the DOM.
     With `priority` plus `loading="eager"`, the AC-23 hero case passed.

